### Restrict Domains

For sensitive environments:

{% if harness == "claude" %}
```yaml
hooks:
  PreToolUse:
    - matcher: "WebFetch|WebSearch"
      hooks:
        - type: command
          command: |
            #!/bin/bash
            # Only allow specific domains
            INPUT=$(cat)
            URL=$(echo "$INPUT" | jq -r '.tool_input.url // empty')
            QUERY=$(echo "$INPUT" | jq -r '.tool_input.query // empty')

            ALLOWED="docs.python.org|reactjs.org|nodejs.org|github.com"

            if [ -n "$URL" ] && ! echo "$URL" | grep -E "$ALLOWED" > /dev/null; then
              echo "Domain not in allowlist" >&2
              exit 2
            fi
            exit 0
```

This illustrates the hook structure only; a substring regex is not a secure domain boundary. Production enforcement must parse and validate URL hosts, redirects, and search destinations. Use a tested validator and host network controls rather than trusting this demonstration.
{% elif harness == "copilot" %}
Use supported host/network policy to restrict destinations and verify redirect behavior. A `tools: [read, search, web]` list does not restrict domains. Do not transplant Claude hooks into the agent file; report when required enforcement is unavailable.
{% else %}
Use the active host's supported network/tool policy to restrict destinations. `sandbox_mode = "read-only"` neither grants web access nor restricts web destinations. Do not copy Claude hook YAML into TOML or claim prompt prose enforces a domain allowlist.
{% endif -%}
